# STYLE DRIFT IS L2 TERRITORY — a PRD can be structurally current (v5.4
# frontmatter, seven sections) and still carry the old §5 bullet list and extra
# §1 bullets. Three assertions, in order:
#   1. the deterministic migrator makes only the mechanical shape edits (§4
#      heading, §1 Success signal bullet, AC1 label) — the rest of the style is
#      never guessed at (exit 1, migrated)
#   2. the opt-in style check names exactly the drift that is left
#   3. the hand-converged file — §5 as the four-column table, §1 back to Who +
#      What changes (its legacy Success signal bullet is tolerated), the auth
#      constraint relocated as an Addressed row and the
#      platform bullet deleted — passes the full 1–6 gate
python3 "$REPO/.claude/scripts/script-prd-update.py" drifted.md
python3 "$REPO/.claude/scripts/script-prd-shape.py" drifted.md --checks 6
python3 "$REPO/.claude/scripts/script-prd-shape.py" converged.md --checks 1,2,3,4,5,6
